<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sfax</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sfax is a port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-gabes">Gulf of Gabès</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a> and the country's second-largest city. It grew in the Aghlabid period, when its walls and Great Mosque were built in the 9th century. The Normans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> held it from 1148 until a revolt in 1156. It is a major centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olive-oil">olive oil</a> production, fishing and trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sfax.jpg" alt="Sfax" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: El Golli Mohamed · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ksar_Berromdhan002.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
